  "modelLimits": "Mapped coordinates, identities, versions and grass/flowerbed tags are source records. Turf colour, blade marks, bloom density, species-neutral petal forms and plant relief are authored estimates. The central red S uses exact flowerbed way/1425123465. The emblem surround and four rose beds are photographic interpretations bounded by the mapped circular path and spokes, with an estimated 1.45 m inward clearance; the central border is 0.32 m wide. Photographs document a historic red/white planting scheme; seasons and later planting replacements vary, so these are not current botanical claims. Geometry carries illustrative relative offsets (turf 0.012 m, flowers 0.16–0.30 m, border 0.12 m); the native terrain ground pass drapes these surfaces onto the DEM and does not retain that vertical relief. Grass blades and blooms are procedural surface detail, not individually modeled plants. Native road/path widths, including estimates, are inherited without reimplementation.",
  "references": [
    {
      "id": "stanford-oval-garden-guide",
      "url": "https://familyweekend.stanford.edu/sites/g/files/sbiybj17671/files/media/file/a_self-guided_tour_of_stanford_gardens.pdf",
      "date": "2017 study republished 2022",
      "observed": "Page 3 describes the broad Oval lawn, round red/white emblem garden, framing rings and symmetric surrounding rose beds. The document cautions that features may have changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "stanford-oval-close-2010",
      "url": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/stanford/oval.html",
      "image": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/stanford/oval/IMG_4109%20bar%20S%20in%20oval%206-14-2010%20stanford%20oval%20Canon%20EOS%20REBEL%20T1i.jpg",
      "date": "2010-06-14",
      "observed": "Inspected original Robert Siegel photograph: low dense red S blooms, white surrounding blooms with visible soil and foliage, low green border. Reference only; no photograph distributed."
    },
    {
      "id": "stanford-oval-flowers-2010",
      "url": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/stanford/oval.html",
      "image": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/stanford/oval/IMG_4105%20oval%20flowers%206-14-2010%20stanford%20oval%20Canon%20EOS%20REBEL%20T1i.jpg",
      "date": "2010-06-14",
      "observed": "Inspected close view shows separate red/white blossom clusters and dark foliage/soil rather than a solid painted floral surface."
    },
    {
      "id": "stanford-oval-aerial-2019",
      "url": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/stanford/1000feet.html",
      "image": "https://web.stanford.edu/~siegelr/flying/heli-flyover2019/0T1A6621%20the%20oval%20-%20stanford%20from%20helicopter%2006-23-2019%20Canon%20EOS%207D%20Mark%20II.jpg",
      "date": "2019-06-23",
      "observed": "Inspected aerial establishes central emblem bed, four surrounding beds, continuous twin linear walks and intervening broad turf. Derived bed extents are estimates inside the mapped path network."
    },
    {
      "id": "stanford-oval-visit",
      "url": "https://www.stanford.edu/life/visit",
      "image": "https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1023936/1200x675/36061dcbd1/stanford-oval-1200w.jpg",
      "observed": "Inspected university visitor photograph shows short fine-textured grass with gradual tonal/mowing variation and clear paths; no flower carpet across the lawn."
    },
    {
      "id": "stanford-planting-seasonality",
      "url": "https://stanforddaily.com/2024/04/24/petal-to-the-metal-wildflowers-bloom-at-stanford/",
      "date": "2024-04-24",
      "observed": "Original report interviewing campus horticulturists describes changes from scarlet Heuchera to red petunias and blue-green fescue around the S; this limits any claim that the historical white-flower surround is current."
    }
